      "path": "app/src/main/java/cloud/samlo/couch/data/Recommendations.kt",
      "content": "The merge took upstream's removal of `backdropUrl = item.image` here. KevBox still uses `backdropUrl`, though: `Tile.kt` and `ProgramTile.kt` deliberately keep it, and `IndexScreen` calls `backdrop.show(card.tile.backdropUrl)` and `backdrop.show(row.entry.programs.firstOrNull()?.backdropUrl)`. `Programs.programs()` puts recommendation tiles into Index channel rows. So on Fire TV, apps that post recommendations instead of preview channels now get `null` and fall back to the wallpaper rather than showing the program's art. That breaks AC-13 for those apps. Put the line back, and add this file to the KevBox-kept list in UPSTREAM-SYNC.md.",
      "suggestion_code": "            imageUrl = item.image,\n            // KevBox: the Index backdrop shows the focused recommendation's art.\n            backdropUrl = item.image,\n            description = item.text,",
      "existing_code": "            imageUrl = item.image,\n            description = item.text,",
      "start_line": 63,
      "end_line": 64,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "release.sh",
      "content": "The script runs under `set -euo pipefail` (line 35). When `KEVBOX_SSH_PORT` is unset, these arrays are empty. On bash older than 4.4 (for example macOS's stock bash 3.2), `\"${arr[@]}\"` on an empty array fails with \"unbound variable\" under `set -u`. The release would then abort at the upload, after the tag and build steps. The same applies to the three `ssh \"${ssh_port_args[@]}\"` calls. The `${arr[@]+\"${arr[@]}\"}` form works on every bash version. The other option is to require bash ≥ 4.4 explicitly.",
      "suggestion_code": "scp ${scp_port_args[@]+\"${scp_port_args[@]}\"} \"$built_apk\" \"$ssh_alias:/tmp/$remote_apk\" || die \"scp failed; version.json was not written\"",
      "existing_code": "scp \"${scp_port_args[@]}\" \"$built_apk\" \"$ssh_alias:/tmp/$remote_apk\" || die \"scp failed; version.json was not written\"",
      "start_line": 222,
      "end_line": 222,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "low"
    },
    {
      "path": ".github/workflows/ci.yml",
      "content": "The budget is now 716800, but AGENTS.md (line 60) still says `ci.yml` gates the APK at Couch's 614400 bytes. Please update that line. Note also that the project gate and release.sh allow 1048576 bytes (AC-35), so a build between 700 KB and 1 MB passes locally and in release.sh but fails CI. If the 700 KB figure is deliberate, document it next to AC-35.",
      "existing_code": "          if [ \"$size\" -gt 716800 ]; then",
      "start_line": 45,
      "end_line": 45,
      "category": "documentation",
      "severity": "low"
    },
