      "path": "app/src/main/java/cloud/samlo/couch/kevbox/drawer/MoveLook.kt",
      "content": "The listener is added to `anchor.viewTreeObserver` when it's registered, but it's removed through whatever `anchor.viewTreeObserver` returns at draw time. If the anchor is detached before that pre-draw (for example, a package broadcast reloads the grid and drops the held card), the getter returns a different floating observer, so the remove call does nothing. The listener then stays on the window's observer and runs on every frame after that: it keeps resetting translations and starting new glides on cards that may already be gone. The usual fix is to capture the observer once and check `isAlive`.",
      "suggestion_code": "        val observer = anchor.viewTreeObserver\n        observer.addOnPreDrawListener(object : ViewTreeObserver.OnPreDrawListener {\n            override fun onPreDraw(): Boolean {\n                if (observer.isAlive) observer.removeOnPreDrawListener(this)\n                else anchor.viewTreeObserver.removeOnPreDrawListener(this)",
      "existing_code": "                anchor.viewTreeObserver.removeOnPreDrawListener(this)",
      "start_line": 59,
